 "text": "Hello! How's everything going? The skin looks orange right after the shower when the blood vessels are still open. It goes away quickly as the makeup settles. Green for green, yellow for yellow, is a useful mnemonic. It doesn't work for every skin tone, so the actual shade may surprise you. It depends how often you wear it. Mixing three or four shades together gives you more skin tones to work with. The skin around the eyes and mouth can be the toughest. Use a little more there, and use a small brush.",
